**Gates before launch**

I save the script below as `spe/evals/harness/r04-workflow.js` and commit it locally. I do not push. I check that `spe/predictions/r04.yaml` matches its commit from 10 minutes ago. Then I run three gates in order and stop at the first one that fails.

1. **Grader selftest.** I turn `answers.json` into output files and run `grade.py` on them. It must score 50 of 50 on both category and priority. It must also fail an empty output and an output with shifted labels. I also check that `answers.json` holds 50 tickets and that `judge.md` exists.
2. **Control.** I regrade round 3's saved outputs with this round's `grade.py` and compare the result to round 3's recorded scores. Any difference means the grader changed. I record that difference before going on.
3. **Dry run.** I launch with `only: ["B:T001", "C2:T002", "C2:T003"]`, `trials: 1`, and `topUpMax: 0`. Every trial must return output that fits its schema. The leak scan must find exactly one driver transcript per trial and no false hits. `grade.py` and the judge must both return values.

I use the dry run's measured costs to set `estTrialUsd` and `estJudgeUsd`. If 500 trials plus 500 judge calls will not fit under $40, I halt and ask you, because the trial count and the cap are your decisions. Otherwise I launch the full run.

```js
export const meta = {
  name: "spe-triage-round",
  description: "SPE eval round for the triage agent. Runs trials per config and ticket, grades labels with code, judges reply tone with Opus, tops up mixed cells, scores predictions, then runs failure analysis and a completeness critic.",
  phases: [
    { title: "Trials" },
    { title: "Grade" },
    { title: "Judge" },
    { title: "Top-up" },
    { title: "Synthesis" },
  ],
};

// Launch args for this round (from spe/plans/r04.md):
// {
//   round: 4,
//   configs: ["B", "C2"],
//   tickets: <the 50 ticket IDs from spe/evals/tasks/answers.json, filled in at launch>,
//   trials: 5,
//   topUpMax: 3,
//   spendCapUsd: 40,
//   estTrialUsd: 0.05,   // estimate, replaced by the dry-run measurement
//   estJudgeUsd: 0.02,   // estimate, replaced by the dry-run measurement
//   runCmd: "python triage/run.py",
//   outDir: "runs/r04",
//   transcriptRoot: "<directory where Workflow agent transcripts are written>"
// }
// Dry run adds: only: ["B:T001", "C2:T002", "C2:T003"], trials: 1, topUpMax: 0
//
// Defaults assumed (the selftest and dry-run gates confirm them):
// - triage/run.py runs one config on one ticket. It writes <out>.json with
//   ticket_text, label.category, label.priority, reply, and metrics. It also
//   writes <out>.transcript.jsonl with the triage agent's messages and tool calls.
// - grade.py takes --answers, --ticket, --output and prints JSON with
//   category_correct and priority_correct.
// - Per-config accuracy uses base trials only. Top-up trials only measure
//   cell stability, so they do not tilt the scored metrics.

// ---------- Arguments ----------
const ROUND = Number(args.round);
if (!Number.isInteger(ROUND) || ROUND < 1) throw new Error("args.round is required");
const RR = String(ROUND).padStart(2, "0");
const NEXT = ROUND + 1;
const CONFIGS = args.configs ?? ["B", "C2"];
const TICKETS = args.tickets ?? [];
const EXPECTED_TICKETS = args.expectedTickets ?? 50;
const TRIALS = args.trials ?? 5;
const TOPUP_MAX = args.topUpMax ?? 3;
const CAP_USD = args.spendCapUsd ?? 40;
const EST_TRIAL_USD = args.estTrialUsd ?? 0.05;
const EST_JUDGE_USD = args.estJudgeUsd ?? 0.02;
const ONLY = args.only ?? null;
const DRIVER_MODEL = args.driverModel ?? "opus";
const JUDGE_MODEL = args.judgeModel ?? "opus";
const RUN_CMD = args.runCmd ?? "python triage/run.py";
const OUT_DIR = args.outDir ?? `runs/r${RR}`;
const TRANSCRIPT_ROOT = args.transcriptRoot;
const PRED_PATH = `spe/predictions/r${RR}.yaml`;
const NONTRIAL = "SPE-NONTRIAL-AGENT";

if (TICKETS.length === 0) throw new Error("args.tickets is required");
if (!TRANSCRIPT_ROOT) throw new Error("args.transcriptRoot is required for the leak scan");
if (!ONLY && TICKETS.length !== EXPECTED_TICKETS) {
  throw new Error(`expected ${EXPECTED_TICKETS} tickets, got ${TICKETS.length}`);
}

// ---------- Halt and budget ----------
let halted = null;
function halt(reason) {
  if (!halted) {
    halted = reason;
    log(`HALT: ${reason}`);
  }
}

const budget = { cap: CAP_USD, spent: 0, reserved: 0, skipped: [] };
function reserve(usd, what) {
  if (halted) {
    budget.skipped.push({ what, reason: `halted: ${halted}` });
    return false;
  }
  if (budget.spent + budget.reserved + usd > budget.cap) {
    budget.skipped.push({ what, reason: `cap $${budget.cap} would be crossed` });
    halt(`spend cap $${budget.cap} reached (spent $${budget.spent.toFixed(2)}, reserved $${budget.reserved.toFixed(2)})`);
    return false;
  }
  budget.reserved += usd;
  return true;
}
function settle(est, actual) {
  budget.reserved -= est;
  budget.spent += typeof actual === "number" ? actual : est;
}

// ---------- Schemas ----------
const TRIAL_SCHEMA = {
  type: "object",
  required: ["status", "category", "priority", "reply_chars", "runtime_s", "tool_calls", "tokens_in", "tokens_out", "tool_errors", "cost_usd"],
  properties: {
    status: { type: "string", enum: ["completed", "harness_error", "rate_limited"] },
    category: { type: ["string", "null"] },
    priority: { type: ["string", "null"] },
    reply_chars: { type: "integer" },
    runtime_s: { type: "number" },
    tool_calls: { type: "integer" },
    tokens_in: { type: "integer" },
    tokens_out: { type: "integer" },
    tool_errors: { type: "integer" },
    cost_usd: { type: "number" },
    error: { type: "string" },
  },
};

const GRADE_SCHEMA = {
  type: "object",
  required: ["transcript_found", "transcript_files", "leak", "grader_ok", "category_correct", "priority_correct"],
  properties: {
    transcript_found: { type: "boolean" },
    transcript_files: { type: "integer" },
    leak: { type: "boolean" },
    leak_evidence: { type: "string" },
    grader_ok: { type: "boolean" },
    grader_error: { type: "string" },
    category_correct: { type: "boolean" },
    priority_correct: { type: "boolean" },
  },
};

const JUDGE_SCHEMA = {
  type: "object",
  required: ["tone_score", "tone_pass", "reason"],
  properties: {
    tone_score: { type: "integer", minimum: 1, maximum: 5 },
    tone_pass: { type: "boolean" },
    reason: { type: "string" },
  },
};

const PRED_SCHEMA = {
  type: "object",
  required: ["rows", "all_hit"],
  properties: {
    rows: {
      type: "array",
      items: {
        type: "object",
        required: ["metric", "config", "predicted", "band", "actual", "result", "grader_check"],
        properties: {
          metric: { type: "string" },
          config: { type: "string" },
          predicted: { type: "number" },
          band: { type: "number" },
          actual: { type: ["number", "null"] },
          result: { type: "string", enum: ["hit", "miss", "not_scorable"] },
          grader_check: { type: "string" },
        },
      },
    },
    all_hit: { type: "boolean" },
    notes: { type: "string" },
  },
};

const FAIL_SCHEMA = {
  type: "object",
  required: ["failures", "proposals"],
  properties: {
    failures: {
      type: "array",
      items: {
        type: "object",
        required: ["id", "title", "configs", "trials", "check", "evidence", "cause"],
        properties: {
          id: { type: "string" },
          title: { type: "string" },
          configs: { type: "array", items: { type: "string" } },
          trials: { type: "array", items: { type: "string" } },
          check: { type: "string" },
          evidence: { type: "string" },
          cause: { type: "string" },
        },
      },
    },
    proposals: { type: "array", items: { type: "string" } },
  },
};

const CRITIC_SCHEMA = {
  type: "object",
  required: ["complete", "gaps"],
  properties: {
    complete: { type: "boolean" },
    gaps: {
      type: "array",
      items: {
        type: "object",
        required: ["issue", "fix"],
        properties: { issue: { type: "string" }, fix: { type: "string" } },
      },
    },
  },
};

// ---------- Items ----------
function trialId(it) {
  return `r${RR}-${it.config}-${it.ticket}-t${it.k}`;
}
function outBase(it) {
  return `${OUT_DIR}/${it.config}/${it.ticket}-t${it.k}`;
}
function buildBaseItems() {
  const items = [];
  for (const config of CONFIGS) {
    for (const ticket of TICKETS) {
      if (ONLY && !ONLY.includes(`${config}:${ticket}`)) continue;
      for (let k = 1; k <= TRIALS; k++) {
        const it = { config, ticket, k, topUp: false };
        items.push({ ...it, id: trialId(it), outBase: outBase(it) });
      }
    }
  }
  return items;
}

// ---------- Prompts ----------
function trialPrompt(t) {
  return `TRIALTAG=[${t.id}]
You drive one eval trial. Run one command, read its output file, and report. Do nothing else.

Run this command once from the repository root:
  ${RUN_CMD} --config ${t.config} --ticket ${t.ticket} --trial ${t.k} --out ${t.outBase}

You may read only files under triage/ and ${OUT_DIR}/. Do not open, list, or search any other path. Do not edit files. Do not retry.

When the command finishes, read ${t.outBase}.json. Copy label.category, label.priority, the reply length in characters, and the metrics fields (runtime_s, tool_calls, tokens_in, tokens_out, tool_errors, cost_usd) into your result.
Set status to "completed" when the triage agent finished and the file exists. Set status to "rate_limited" when the command failed on a rate limit or overload. Set status to "harness_error" for any other failure, and put the message in error.`;
}

function gradePrompt(t) {
  return `${NONTRIAL}
You grade one trial with code. Do not judge reply quality.
Trial: ${t.id}. Output files: ${t.outBase}.json and ${t.outBase}.transcript.jsonl.

Step 1. Find the driver transcript. Run:
  grep -rlF "TRIALTAG=[${t.id}]" ${TRANSCRIPT_ROOT} | while read f; do grep -qF "${NONTRIAL}" "$f" || echo "$f"; done
Exactly one file is expected. Set transcript_files to the count. Set transcript_found to true only when the count is 1.

Step 2. Leak scan. In the driver transcript and in ${t.outBase}.transcript.jsonl, look for "spe/evals/" or "spe/predictions/" inside tool call inputs. Tool call inputs are Read paths, Grep or Glob patterns and paths, and Bash commands. Ignore tool output text. Set leak to true on any hit and put the first hit in leak_evidence.

Step 3. Run:
  python spe/evals/graders/grade.py --answers spe/evals/tasks/answers.json --ticket ${t.ticket} --output ${t.outBase}.json
Copy category_correct and priority_correct from its JSON output. If it exits nonzero or prints invalid JSON, set grader_ok to false, set both checks to false, and put the error in grader_error.`;
}

function judgePrompt(t) {
  return `${NONTRIAL}
You judge the tone of one drafted support reply.
Read spe/evals/graders/judge.md and apply its rubric exactly.
Read ${t.outBase}.json. Use only its ticket_text and reply fields. Do not read the label, spe/evals/tasks/answers.json, anything under spe/predictions/, or any other trial.
Judge tone only. Code grades category and priority elsewhere.
Return the rubric score from 1 to 5, whether the reply meets the rubric's pass line, and one sentence of reason that quotes the reply.`;
}

// ---------- Stages ----------
async function runTrial(t) {
  if (!reserve(EST_TRIAL_USD, `trial ${t.id}`)) return { ...t, status: "skipped" };
  let r;
  try {
    r = await agent(trialPrompt(t), {
      label: `trial ${t.id}`,
      phase: t.topUp ? "Top-up" : "Trials",
      schema: TRIAL_SCHEMA,
      model: DRIVER_MODEL,
    });
  } catch (e) {
    settle(EST_TRIAL_USD, EST_TRIAL_USD);
    return { ...t, status: "harness_error", error: String(e) };
  }
  settle(EST_TRIAL_USD, r.cost_usd);
  return { ...t, ...r };
}

async function gradeTrial(t) {
  if (t.status !== "completed") return t;
  if (halted && halted.startsWith("broken grader")) return { ...t, graded: false };
  let g;
  try {
    g = await agent(gradePrompt(t), { label: `grade ${t.id}`, phase: "Grade", schema: GRADE_SCHEMA, model: DRIVER_MODEL });
  } catch (e) {
    halt(`broken grader on ${t.id}: ${String(e)}`);
    return { ...t, graded: false };
  }
  if (!g.transcript_found) {
    halt(`leak scan found ${g.transcript_files} driver transcripts for ${t.id}, expected 1`);
    return { ...t, graded: false, voided: true, void_reason: "leak scan unverified" };
  }
  if (g.leak) {
    halt(`leaked answer key: ${t.id} touched ${g.leak_evidence}`);
    return { ...t, graded: false, voided: true, void_reason: `peeked: ${g.leak_evidence}` };
  }
  if (!g.grader_ok) {
    halt(`broken grader on ${t.id}: ${g.grader_error}`);
    return { ...t, graded: false };
  }
  return {
    ...t,
    graded: true,
    category_correct: g.category_correct,
    priority_correct: g.priority_correct,
    label_pass: g.category_correct && g.priority_correct,
  };
}

async function judgeTrial(t) {
  if (!t.graded || t.voided) return t;
  if (!reserve(EST_JUDGE_USD, `judge ${t.id}`)) return { ...t, judged: false };
  try {
    const j = await agent(judgePrompt(t), { label: `judge ${t.id}`, phase: "Judge", schema: JUDGE_SCHEMA, model: JUDGE_MODEL });
    settle(EST_JUDGE_USD, EST_JUDGE_USD);
    return { ...t, judged: true, tone_score: j.tone_score, tone_pass: j.tone_pass, tone_reason: j.reason };
  } catch (e) {
    settle(EST_JUDGE_USD, EST_JUDGE_USD);
    return { ...t, judged: false, judge_error: String(e) };
  }
}

// ---------- Aggregation ----------
const countable = (t) => t.status === "completed" && t.graded === true && !t.voided;
const mean = (xs) => (xs.length ? xs.reduce((a, b) => a + b, 0) / xs.length : null);
const rate = (xs, f) => mean(xs.map((t) => (f(t) ? 1 : 0)));

function cellKey(t) {
  return `${t.config}:${t.ticket}`;
}
function groupCells(rs) {
  const m = new Map();
  for (const t of rs) {
    const key = cellKey(t);
    if (!m.has(key)) m.set(key, []);
    m.get(key).push(t);
  }
  return m;
}

function summarize(rs, config) {
  const all = rs.filter((t) => t.config === config);
  const base = all.filter((t) => !t.topUp);
  const c = base.filter(countable);
  const judged = c.filter((t) => t.judged);
  return {
    config,
    attempted: all.length,
    base_completed: c.length,
    harness_errors: all.filter((t) => t.status === "harness_error").length,
    rate_limited: all.filter((t) => t.status === "rate_limited").length,
    voided: all.filter((t) => t.voided).length,
    skipped: all.filter((t) => t.status === "skipped").length,
    category_accuracy: rate(c, (t) => t.category_correct),
    priority_accuracy: rate(c, (t) => t.priority_correct),
    label_accuracy: rate(c, (t) => t.label_pass),
    tone_pass_rate: rate(judged, (t) => t.tone_pass),
    tone_mean: mean(judged.map((t) => t.tone_score)),
    runtime_s_mean: mean(c.map((t) => t.runtime_s)),
    tool_calls_mean: mean(c.map((t) => t.tool_calls)),
    tokens_mean: mean(c.map((t) => t.tokens_in + t.tokens_out)),
    tool_errors_mean: mean(c.map((t) => t.tool_errors)),
    cost_usd_mean: mean(c.map((t) => t.cost_usd)),
  };
}

function cellTable(rs) {
  const rows = [];
  for (const [key, ts] of groupCells(rs)) {
    const baseC = ts.filter((t) => !t.topUp && countable(t));
    const allC = ts.filter(countable);
    rows.push({
      cell: key,
      base: `${baseC.filter((t) => t.label_pass).length}/${baseC.length}`,
      with_topup: `${allC.filter((t) => t.label_pass).length}/${allC.length}`,
    });
  }
  return rows;
}

// ---------- Run ----------
log(`Round ${ROUND}: configs ${CONFIGS.join(", ")}, ${TICKETS.length} tickets, ${TRIALS} trials per cell, cap $${CAP_USD}${ONLY ? `, dry run on ${ONLY.join(", ")}` : ""}`);
log("Judge note: the tone judge is Opus, the same family as the Sonnet trials. No cross-family judge is available, so tone scores may share blind spots with the agent.");

phase("Trials");
const baseItems = buildBaseItems();
log(`${baseItems.length} base trials queued`);
let results = await pipeline(baseItems, runTrial, gradeTrial, judgeTrial);

phase("Top-up");
if (halted) {
  log(`Top-up skipped. Halted: ${halted}`);
} else if (TOPUP_MAX > 0) {
  const topUpItems = [];
  for (const [, ts] of groupCells(results)) {
    const c = ts.filter(countable);
    const passes = c.filter((t) => t.label_pass).length;
    if (passes > 0 && passes < c.length) {
      const maxK = Math.max(...ts.map((t) => t.k));
      for (let j = 1; j <= TOPUP_MAX; j++) {
        const it = { config: ts[0].config, ticket: ts[0].ticket, k: maxK + j, topUp: true };
        topUpItems.push({ ...it, id: trialId(it), outBase: outBase(it) });
      }
    }
  }
  log(`${topUpItems.length} top-up trials queued for mixed cells (cap ${TOPUP_MAX} per cell)`);
  if (topUpItems.length > 0) {
    const more = await pipeline(topUpItems, runTrial, gradeTrial, judgeTrial);
    results = results.concat(more);
  }
}

phase("Synthesis");
const configSummaries = CONFIGS.map((c) => summarize(results, c));
const scoredMetrics = ["category_accuracy", "priority_accuracy", "label_accuracy", "tone_pass_rate"];
const saturated = scoredMetrics.filter((m) => configSummaries.every((s) => s[m] === 1));
if (saturated.length > 0) log(`Ceiling: every config scored 1.0 on ${saturated.join(", ")}. Those predictions are not scorable.`);

const summary = {
  round: ROUND,
  expected_base_trials: baseItems.length,
  configs: configSummaries,
  cells: cellTable(results),
  saturated,
  budget: { cap: budget.cap, spent: Number(budget.spent.toFixed(2)), skipped: budget.skipped },
  halted,
};

if (halted) {
  log("Synthesis agents skipped because the run halted. Report the halt to the user.");
  return { round: ROUND, halted, summary };
}

const failing = results
  .filter((t) => (countable(t) && (!t.label_pass || t.tone_pass === false)) || t.status === "harness_error" || t.status === "rate_limited")
  .map((t) => `${t.id} ${t.outBase}.json status=${t.status} cat=${t.category_correct ?? "-"} pri=${t.priority_correct ?? "-"} tone=${t.tone_pass ?? "-"}`)
  .join("\n");

const pred = await agent(`${NONTRIAL}
You score this round's predictions against measured results.
Read ${PRED_PATH}. Do not edit it.
For each metric and config cell, report the predicted value, the band, the actual value from the summary below, and the grader check named in the file.
A cell is a hit when the actual value lies within predicted plus or minus band. Mark metrics in this list as not_scorable: ${JSON.stringify(saturated)}.
Accuracy metrics come from base trials only. Harness errors, rate limits, voided trials, and skipped trials are excluded.
Summary:
${JSON.stringify(summary)}`, { label: "score predictions", phase: "Synthesis", schema: PRED_SCHEMA, model: "opus" });

const fail = await agent(`${NONTRIAL}
You analyze failures for round ${ROUND} of the triage eval.
Read each listed output file and spe/evals/tasks/answers.json. Group the failures by cause. Name each group with an ID of the form "r${RR} F1", "r${RR} F2", and so on.
For each group, give the configs, the trial IDs, the check that failed (category, priority, tone, or harness), concrete evidence quoted from the outputs, and the likely cause.
Treat harness errors and rate limits as harness failures, not model failures.
If any metric saturated (${JSON.stringify(saturated)}), log the saturation as a failure and propose harder tasks.
End with proposals for what round ${NEXT} should change. Each proposal changes one thing.
Prediction results:
${JSON.stringify(pred)}
Summary:
${JSON.stringify(summary)}
Failing trials:
${failing || "(none)"}`, { label: "failure analysis", phase: "Synthesis", schema: FAIL_SCHEMA, model: "opus" });

const critic = await agent(`${NONTRIAL}
You are the completeness critic for round ${ROUND} of the triage eval. Check the outputs below and list every gap with a fix.
Check these points:
- Base trials attempted equal ${baseItems.length}. Every skip has a logged reason.
- No voided trial counts toward any metric.
- Harness errors and rate limits are excluded from accuracy.
- Every prediction row in ${PRED_PATH} has a result.
- Every failure ID cites trial IDs and evidence.
- Every proposal for round ${NEXT} changes one thing.
- The report notes that the tone judge is the same model family as the trials.
- Spend stayed under $${CAP_USD}.
Summary:
${JSON.stringify(summary)}
Prediction results:
${JSON.stringify(pred)}
Failure analysis:
${JSON.stringify(fail)}`, { label: "completeness critic", phase: "Synthesis", schema: CRITIC_SCHEMA, model: "opus" });

log(`Predictions all hit: ${pred.all_hit}. Failures: ${fail.failures.length}. Critic complete: ${critic.complete}. Spent $${budget.spent.toFixed(2)} of $${CAP_USD}.`);

return { round: ROUND, halted: null, summary, predictions: pred, failures: fail, critic };
```
